1
00:00:09,414 --> 00:00:15,424
Episode 12

2
00:00:09,414 --> 00:00:15,424
Episode 12

3
00:00:09,414 --> 00:00:15,424
The Starry Bridge that Leads to the Night Sky

4
00:00:09,414 --> 00:00:15,424
The Starry Bridge that Leads to the Night Sky

5
00:00:12,604 --> 00:00:13,504
Eh?!

6
00:00:13,504 --> 00:00:15,424
I'm playing the role of the Ogami in the festival?

7
00:00:16,274 --> 00:00:17,794
How did that happen?

8
00:00:18,154 --> 00:00:20,324
You didn't know?

9
00:00:20,324 --> 00:00:26,614
The winner of the Hikonan Race is assigned the role of the Ogami for that year.

10
00:00:27,354 --> 00:00:29,624
Didn't I tell you?

11
00:00:29,624 --> 00:00:31,244
I never heard anything like that.

12
00:00:31,244 --> 00:00:35,314
Anyway, didn't Koyori win the race?

13
00:00:35,984 --> 00:00:39,494
No matter how much of a tomboy Koyori-chan is, she's still a girl.

14
00:00:39,494 --> 00:00:41,864
She obviously isn't suitable for the role of the Ogami, right?

15
00:00:41,864 --> 00:00:44,004
Well, I suppose so.

16
00:00:45,224 --> 00:00:49,834
You're the runner-up, Kazuma-kun, so you're going to do it.

17
00:00:49,834 --> 00:00:55,504
Fate has chosen you as our participant, so please do your best.

18
00:00:55,964 --> 00:00:57,134
Okay...

19
00:00:57,584 --> 00:00:59,334
But is it really okay?

20
00:00:59,334 --> 00:01:03,424
A person like me, from the big city, playing such an important role?

21
00:01:03,424 --> 00:01:05,204
What are you talking about?

22
00:01:05,204 --> 00:01:07,264
We're more than happy to have you for this, actually!

23
00:01:07,264 --> 00:01:13,004
Although this festival is for celebrating the legend of the Twin Mountains,

24
00:01:13,004 --> 00:01:18,894
to be the helper of the gods, or basically, taking in other people from other towns,

25
00:01:18,894 --> 00:01:23,114
is considered a divine blessing.

26
00:01:29,194 --> 00:01:34,194
That's why we're hoping people like you, Kazuma-kun,

27
00:01:34,194 --> 00:01:37,294
will come to our town to play the Ogami role
and create a fresh new batch of descendants.

28
00:01:40,354 --> 00:01:42,384
What are you talking about so early in the morning?!

29
00:01:42,384 --> 00:01:44,384
Onii-chan, what does "descendants" mean?

30
00:01:45,784 --> 00:01:47,264
Well, that's...

31
00:01:47,764 --> 00:01:51,014
Ayumu-kun, a descendant is-

32
00:01:51,334 --> 00:01:52,674
Nee-san!

33
00:01:56,844 --> 00:01:59,444
Must be nice, playing the role of the Ogami.

34
00:01:59,444 --> 00:02:00,904
You really think so?

35
00:02:00,904 --> 00:02:04,124
Hey, the Megami is played by Tsumugi-san, you know.

36
00:02:04,124 --> 00:02:07,384
That poyoyon poyoyon tapun tapun...!

37
00:02:07,384 --> 00:02:09,774
That's all you think about, huh?

38
00:02:09,774 --> 00:02:13,954
Hey Bro, how about you take this chance and confess your love?

39
00:02:15,584 --> 00:02:17,004
Why do I have to do that?!

40
00:02:17,394 --> 00:02:18,714
Didn't you know?

41
00:02:18,714 --> 00:02:26,254
In the past, the Ogami was allowed to confess to the Megami during the calling-out ceremony.

42
00:02:26,664 --> 00:02:27,284
Eh?

43
00:02:27,284 --> 00:02:28,594
I see.

44
00:02:29,304 --> 00:02:36,754
Tsumugi-san is great, but normally the one chosen for the role of Megami is the most beautiful girl in town.

45
00:02:36,754 --> 00:02:42,614
Of course, there are guys who would want to make their move on her,

46
00:02:42,614 --> 00:02:49,614
and in fact, the Hikonan Race was originally
founded as a way to fight for the right to confess.

47
00:02:50,004 --> 00:02:51,114
Really?

48
00:02:51,694 --> 00:03:00,174
A few generations ago, there were quite a few cases where the Megami and the Ogami ended up together because of this.

49
00:03:00,174 --> 00:03:04,534
There's even a rumour that those who have confessed their love...

50
00:03:04,534 --> 00:03:07,174
...and become a couple because of the race will bring about a good harvest year.

51
00:03:07,174 --> 00:03:10,384
But why do I have to confess to Tsumugi-san?

52
00:03:10,714 --> 00:03:12,304
Good morning!

53
00:03:12,304 --> 00:03:13,874
What are you two discussing so early in the morning?

54
00:03:13,874 --> 00:03:15,674
What's up with Tsumugi-san?

55
00:03:15,674 --> 00:03:17,264
Ah, it's nothing...

56
00:03:17,894 --> 00:03:18,764
Good morning!

57
00:03:20,224 --> 00:03:22,734
Ah... good morning.

58
00:03:32,994 --> 00:03:37,414
Geez, my mum talks so much. She never stops!

59
00:03:38,334 --> 00:03:40,294
Bro, you have anything planned today?

60
00:03:40,294 --> 00:03:42,584
Shall we all go to Backpipe?

61
00:03:42,584 --> 00:03:43,754
I'll pass.

62
00:03:43,754 --> 00:03:44,884
I've got club activities.

63
00:03:44,884 --> 00:03:45,674
Me too.

64
00:03:45,674 --> 00:03:48,714
I have to attend a meeting at the shrine.

65
00:03:49,264 --> 00:03:50,924
So that means Ui, too?

66
00:03:50,924 --> 00:03:52,974
Y-Yup, that's right.

67
00:03:52,974 --> 00:03:55,054
Tch. Can't be helped.

68
00:03:55,054 --> 00:03:57,474
I'll just go grab a bite and head home then.

69
00:03:57,474 --> 00:04:01,184
If you're feeling lonely, I'll accompany you.

70
00:04:01,894 --> 00:04:04,694
Since the festival is coming up, you must be in a festive mood.

71
00:04:05,734 --> 00:04:07,524
I'll quench that thirst for fun you've got!

72
00:04:07,904 --> 00:04:11,444
We shall have a face-to-face talk with each other!

73
00:04:18,994 --> 00:04:23,584
Well, it sure was a surprise to hear
that I was going to play the Ogami.

74
00:04:23,584 --> 00:04:25,424
I guess so.

75
00:04:25,424 --> 00:04:27,384
I would've been surprised, too.

76
00:04:37,644 --> 00:04:38,554
Um...

77
00:04:37,644 --> 00:04:38,554
Erm...

78
00:04:39,014 --> 00:04:39,814
What is it?

79
00:04:39,814 --> 00:04:41,064
Well, you see...

80
00:04:41,064 --> 00:04:42,734
You first.

81
00:04:43,234 --> 00:04:45,274
It's nothing.

82
00:04:58,204 --> 00:05:00,244
There's no conversation.

83
00:05:03,374 --> 00:05:04,714
When did you show up?

84
00:05:04,714 --> 00:05:06,214
At least tell us you're there!

85
00:05:16,554 --> 00:05:17,764
What's wrong?

86
00:05:17,764 --> 00:05:19,644
If we don't hurry, we'll be late.

87
00:05:34,114 --> 00:05:35,154
Wow!

88
00:05:35,154 --> 00:05:37,034
Amazing! It suits you, Onii-san!

89
00:05:37,034 --> 00:05:39,034
You look really handsome.

90
00:05:40,034 --> 00:05:41,124
Thank you...

91
00:05:41,704 --> 00:05:43,334
Then, I'll be taking a shot!

92
00:05:44,664 --> 00:05:45,294
Eh?

93
00:05:45,794 --> 00:05:49,084
Kasane-chan, I don't mind the photos, but why are you here?

94
00:05:49,384 --> 00:05:51,344
I'm collecting data!

95
00:05:51,344 --> 00:05:53,954
As the "Fast Eared Girl" of Yamabiko Town,

96
00:05:53,954 --> 00:05:56,844
I can't just pass up such juicy information!

97
00:05:57,344 --> 00:05:59,744
Ah, for your information,

98
00:05:59,744 --> 00:06:06,274
I'm not taking Mugi-nee's photo to sell to the Koutobu brothers.

99
00:06:06,274 --> 00:06:08,274
I'm totally not doing that.

100
00:06:09,274 --> 00:06:11,114
Sorry to have kept you waiting!

101
00:06:26,164 --> 00:06:27,294
Wow!

102
00:06:27,294 --> 00:06:28,754
Mugi-nee, you're beautiful!

103
00:06:28,754 --> 00:06:30,504
Thank you, Kasane-chan.

104
00:06:30,504 --> 00:06:34,674
Hina-senpai and Nakatsugawa-senpai both
look like shrine maidens. They're great, too!

105
00:06:46,774 --> 00:06:47,644
Sorry to have kept you waiting.

106
00:06:47,644 --> 00:06:49,274
The tea is here.

107
00:06:50,564 --> 00:06:54,024
Sorry to have you help us, when you're a guest.

108
00:06:54,024 --> 00:06:54,904
It's nothing.

109
00:06:57,444 --> 00:06:59,784
You weren't used to that outfit, so you must be tired.

110
00:06:59,784 --> 00:07:01,414
Ah, not really.

111
00:07:02,624 --> 00:07:04,454
Where's Nakatsugawa-senpai?

112
00:07:04,454 --> 00:07:05,664
She's in the washroom.

113
00:07:05,664 --> 00:07:08,664
She said that since she had to stay in full dress, she was holding it all this time.

114
00:07:09,004 --> 00:07:11,674
My, she should have just said so.

115
00:07:11,674 --> 00:07:14,344
Excuse me, I need to go to the washroom, too.

116
00:07:17,054 --> 00:07:21,764
That reminds me, Koumoto-senpai is playing the role of the Angel this year, right?

117
00:07:21,764 --> 00:07:25,764
Yes. That's why I've been busy practising every day.

118
00:07:25,764 --> 00:07:28,274
Won't you model your outfit for us?

119
00:07:28,274 --> 00:07:31,484
I could, but it doesn't have to be now...

120
00:07:31,484 --> 00:07:34,364
I want to see Senpai wearing that outfit!

121
00:07:36,404 --> 00:07:37,114
I know!

122
00:07:37,114 --> 00:07:41,784
Since we're at it, do you mind striking a
pose and letting me take a photo of you?

123
00:07:42,114 --> 00:07:43,614
Isn't that good?

124
00:07:43,614 --> 00:07:46,284
You'll have to show yourself in that outfit anyway.

125
00:07:46,284 --> 00:07:48,494
Then it's decided!

126
00:07:48,494 --> 00:07:51,624
After we finish eating our bean jelly, let's go and get you changed!

127
00:07:51,624 --> 00:07:52,874
Eh?!

128
00:07:55,794 --> 00:07:56,634
Ui-chan.

129
00:07:58,004 --> 00:07:59,464
Tsumugi-san..

130
00:08:00,384 --> 00:08:02,264
Could I talk to you for a bit?

131
00:08:05,554 --> 00:08:09,394
Ui-chan, did you have a fight with Kazuma-san?

132
00:08:11,814 --> 00:08:13,644
Then, why?

133
00:08:13,644 --> 00:08:19,204
I noticed that something is different between you and Kazuma-san.

134
00:08:19,204 --> 00:08:21,034
That's...

135
00:08:22,574 --> 00:08:24,034
I'm sorry.

136
00:08:24,034 --> 00:08:26,284
If you don't want to tell me, I won't force-

137
00:08:26,284 --> 00:08:28,284
I realised.

138
00:08:28,284 --> 00:08:29,034
Eh?

139
00:08:29,494 --> 00:08:35,044
I've been thinking about Kazu-kun being
like a brother to me, and because of that,

140
00:08:35,044 --> 00:08:40,094
when I'm with him, I always have fun, and I get soft, warm feelings of happiness.

141
00:08:40,424 --> 00:08:41,304
But...

142
00:08:41,594 --> 00:08:47,144
But, my brother is my brother, and I realised that Kazu-kun isn't him.

143
00:08:47,144 --> 00:08:51,314
And then, I couldn't find a way to speak normally to Kazu-kun.

144
00:08:51,814 --> 00:08:55,394
When our eyes make contact, my chest tightens suddenly,

145
00:08:55,394 --> 00:09:01,824
and when I'm alone at home, all I think about is Kazu-kun and my cheeks get all hot...

146
00:09:03,824 --> 00:09:06,534
Ui-chan, that's love.

147
00:09:06,914 --> 00:09:07,994
No!

148
00:09:07,994 --> 00:09:09,874
That's not true!

149
00:09:09,874 --> 00:09:11,494
That's not true...

150
00:09:11,494 --> 00:09:15,334
It's just that my heart races when I think about Kazu-kun.

151
00:09:15,334 --> 00:09:19,044
It's not l-love or anything!

152
00:09:19,044 --> 00:09:23,464
It's... It's totally different. I mean...

153
00:09:25,474 --> 00:09:28,464
Ui and Tsumugi-san are really taking a while.

154
00:09:28,464 --> 00:09:29,604
I wonder what happened.

155
00:09:30,684 --> 00:09:31,854
Hoshino.

156
00:09:31,854 --> 00:09:34,644
Why didn't you tell Ui that she was cute?

157
00:09:36,314 --> 00:09:38,444
Where did that question come from?!

158
00:09:38,444 --> 00:09:41,864
Hoshino, you thought Ui was cute when you looked at her,

159
00:09:41,864 --> 00:09:43,904
but you didn't say it.

160
00:09:44,204 --> 00:09:45,114
Why?

161
00:09:47,114 --> 00:09:48,744
"Why?" you ask...

162
00:09:50,074 --> 00:09:53,874
That time when I left my house and my dad came to bring me back,

163
00:09:53,874 --> 00:09:58,004
Hoshino, you helped me say what I wanted to say.

164
00:10:00,334 --> 00:10:03,804
Back then, I was really happy.

165
00:10:04,174 --> 00:10:12,104
But after that, I realised that I had to say what I wanted to say on my own.

166
00:10:13,814 --> 00:10:21,494
I had always wanted to apologise for
misunderstanding and getting angry at you.

167
00:10:21,494 --> 00:10:27,244
That's why I was really happy when I finally managed to apologise to you properly.

168
00:10:27,994 --> 00:10:32,374
Hoshino, if you have something you want to say, you should speak up about it.

169
00:10:33,164 --> 00:10:34,834
Senpai.

170
00:10:40,254 --> 00:10:42,964
Ui-chan, that's love.

171
00:10:43,674 --> 00:10:45,304
Love, huh?

172
00:10:49,554 --> 00:10:50,764
That's...

173
00:10:50,764 --> 00:10:52,974
I don't even know, myself.

174
00:10:53,354 --> 00:10:54,514
Love...

175
00:10:54,514 --> 00:10:56,814
I don't even know what it is.

176
00:11:03,484 --> 00:11:05,574
That's the third time you've yawned this morning.

177
00:11:05,574 --> 00:11:06,944
What happened?

178
00:11:06,944 --> 00:11:09,364
I was up late last night.

179
00:11:09,744 --> 00:11:10,954
Are you all right?

180
00:11:10,954 --> 00:11:13,244
Don't you have to practise for the festival after school?

181
00:11:14,624 --> 00:11:15,704
Yup.

182
00:11:15,704 --> 00:11:20,964
I'll sleep during lunch break. I'll be fine.

183
00:11:23,044 --> 00:11:27,094
Well then, I'll make a brief run-through of the festival procedure.

184
00:11:27,094 --> 00:11:30,344
I'll be more detailed about the difficult parts during the practice sessions,

185
00:11:30,344 --> 00:11:33,844
so please try to get a general idea of the procedures.

186
00:11:34,304 --> 00:11:39,104
First, Madoka will be playing the Angel and will arrive in the human realm.

187
00:11:40,184 --> 00:11:46,484
After that, the Ogami, waiting at the bottom of the steps, will receive the scroll from the Angel.

188
00:11:47,364 --> 00:11:52,074
Next, the Ogami will descend the flight of stone steps, and ride the carriage waiting at the bottom.

189
00:11:52,614 --> 00:11:58,124
The Megami will change into the ceremonial clothes and stand by with the two Arks.

190
00:11:58,874 --> 00:12:02,924
Tsumugi-chan has experience with the Ark role, so this part should be fine for you, right?

191
00:12:03,334 --> 00:12:04,124
Yes.

192
00:12:04,584 --> 00:12:10,344
After the Ogami's carriage has started moving, we will contact you, and at the arranged time,

193
00:12:10,344 --> 00:12:13,054
the Megami and the Arks will set off.

194
00:12:13,514 --> 00:12:17,854
When you reach the bridge, they will start playing the taiko,

195
00:12:17,854 --> 00:12:20,604
which signals the start of the calling-out ceremony.

196
00:12:20,604 --> 00:12:23,814
The Ogami will read the scroll he received from the Angel,

197
00:12:23,814 --> 00:12:28,524
while the Megami will read the scroll she received from the Arks.

198
00:12:28,944 --> 00:12:32,904
Every year, the scrolls are written by the Angel, aren't they?

199
00:12:33,284 --> 00:12:34,204
Yes.

200
00:12:34,204 --> 00:12:38,034
Using dew collected on the morning of the festival, I make ink and write the scrolls.

201
00:12:38,334 --> 00:12:42,044
So, Koumoto-senpai can write those squiggly words!

202
00:12:42,414 --> 00:12:44,214
Erm, one question...

203
00:12:44,214 --> 00:12:45,504
What is it, Kazuma-kun?

204
00:12:45,834 --> 00:12:49,214
"Those squiggly words" refers to the words on the scrolls, right?

205
00:12:49,214 --> 00:12:51,714
I can't read any of those words at all.

206
00:12:51,714 --> 00:12:53,224
It'll be fine.

207
00:12:53,224 --> 00:12:58,264
For both scrolls, the furigana for the words will be written on the remaining space in the scrolls.

208
00:12:58,644 --> 00:13:00,264
Oh, I see...

209
00:13:00,264 --> 00:13:01,524
Are you relieved?

210
00:13:01,524 --> 00:13:02,274
Yes.

211
00:13:02,274 --> 00:13:03,644
If all I have to do is read what's written.

212
00:13:04,274 --> 00:13:06,484
That's why you have to keep your cool.

213
00:13:06,854 --> 00:13:09,274
Even though you're just reading from the scroll,

214
00:13:09,274 --> 00:13:11,864
if you bring out your feelings while saying those words,

215
00:13:11,864 --> 00:13:15,364
it will become a statement of truth to the Megami.

216
00:13:15,694 --> 00:13:21,054
If you bring out your feelings while saying those words, it will become a statement of truth.

217
00:13:21,054 --> 00:13:21,834
Ah!

218
00:13:27,254 --> 00:13:33,264
So here, I shake it twice, spin around, and after that-

219
00:13:33,714 --> 00:13:34,554
Hmm?

220
00:13:34,554 --> 00:13:35,634
Hello-

221
00:13:41,014 --> 00:13:42,474
Hello?

222
00:13:43,224 --> 00:13:44,734
Tsumugi-senpai?

223
00:13:45,934 --> 00:13:46,524
Eh?

224
00:13:46,524 --> 00:13:47,944
You want to pretend that you're sick?

225
00:13:48,814 --> 00:13:50,944
Hoshizora e Kakaru Hashi

226
00:13:48,814 --> 00:13:50,944
Hoshizora e Kakaru Hashi

227
00:13:51,824 --> 00:13:53,944
Hoshizora e Kakaru Hashi

228
00:13:51,824 --> 00:13:53,944
Hoshizora e Kakaru Hashi

229
00:14:47,584 --> 00:14:50,044
Yamabiko Community Centre

230
00:14:53,754 --> 00:14:55,714
Sign: Megami Resting Room

231
00:14:57,304 --> 00:15:01,394
It's about time. They said that you should go and change.

232
00:15:01,724 --> 00:15:02,644
Ah, okay!

233
00:15:02,644 --> 00:15:03,724
Then...

234
00:15:07,774 --> 00:15:09,104
Mugi-nee, what's wrong?

235
00:15:09,484 --> 00:15:10,984
My stomach...

236
00:15:10,984 --> 00:15:12,654
My stomach suddenly...

237
00:15:12,654 --> 00:15:13,234
Eh?!

238
00:15:13,234 --> 00:15:14,864
Ah, we need a doctor...

239
00:15:14,864 --> 00:15:16,074
No, call an ambulance!

240
00:15:16,614 --> 00:15:18,784
I'm fine, Ui-chan.

241
00:15:18,784 --> 00:15:23,534
If I rest, it should go away.

242
00:15:23,994 --> 00:15:24,994
But...

243
00:15:25,334 --> 00:15:27,874
More importantly, the Megami role...

244
00:15:27,874 --> 00:15:28,834
It's impossible, Mugi-nee.

245
00:15:29,204 --> 00:15:31,674
It would be better to ask for a replacement.

246
00:15:32,254 --> 00:15:35,044
Ui-chan, could you do it for me?

247
00:15:35,044 --> 00:15:35,674
Eh?!

248
00:15:35,674 --> 00:15:37,134
I can't do it!

249
00:15:37,134 --> 00:15:39,594
Asking me to be the Megami out of the blue...

250
00:15:39,594 --> 00:15:44,854
Ui-chan, since you've been practising with me for so long, you should know the procedure, right?

251
00:15:46,304 --> 00:15:48,724
Just do it as you're supposed to.

252
00:15:49,104 --> 00:15:51,774
That's why, please...

253
00:15:52,354 --> 00:15:56,444
But, if I do that, then we'll be one Ark short...

254
00:15:56,444 --> 00:15:58,534
That's fine.

255
00:15:59,034 --> 00:16:02,114
There's a replacement Ark here.

256
00:16:06,704 --> 00:16:07,414
Eh?!

257
00:16:07,414 --> 00:16:08,544
Me?!

258
00:16:08,544 --> 00:16:09,914
Impossible, impossible, impossible!

259
00:16:10,624 --> 00:16:15,004
Kasane has been taking photos of us practising for quite a while.

260
00:16:15,004 --> 00:16:18,384
You should be familiar with the procedure, too.

261
00:16:18,384 --> 00:16:21,174
I guess so.

262
00:16:21,674 --> 00:16:23,264
It's an emergency!

263
00:16:28,224 --> 00:16:32,184
"Do it", or "Please do it": Take your pick!

264
00:16:33,144 --> 00:16:35,024
Please let me do it!

265
00:18:42,194 --> 00:18:43,694
Onii-chan, concentrate!

266
00:19:00,834 --> 00:19:03,794
I love you, Ui

267
00:19:18,224 --> 00:19:20,894
Even though you're just reading from the scroll,

268
00:19:20,894 --> 00:19:23,484
if you bring out your feelings while saying those words,

269
00:19:23,484 --> 00:19:27,114
it will become a statement of truth to the Megami.

270
00:19:27,484 --> 00:19:32,114
Hoshino, if you have something you want to say, you should speak up about it.

271
00:19:36,584 --> 00:19:40,964
I love you, Ui

272
00:19:44,084 --> 00:19:50,144
Although it might not have been from the moment we met, when I realised it,

273
00:19:50,144 --> 00:19:53,894
when I was with you, well...

274
00:19:54,644 --> 00:19:58,934
Anyway, I love you

275
00:20:05,564 --> 00:20:06,274
Ui!

276
00:20:06,274 --> 00:20:07,864
What's your reply?

277
00:20:08,194 --> 00:20:10,364
I.. I...

278
00:20:10,364 --> 00:20:11,654
I can't hear you!

279
00:20:11,654 --> 00:20:13,284
Say it louder!

280
00:20:13,824 --> 00:20:17,034
I... Kazu-kun... too...

281
00:20:17,374 --> 00:20:18,544
Louder, Ui!

282
00:20:21,454 --> 00:20:24,674
I love Kazu-kun, too!

283
00:20:25,294 --> 00:20:30,764
I love you. I love you. I really love you!

284
00:20:30,714 --> 00:20:38,104
futari de mita haruka kanata no ryuusei

285
00:20:30,714 --> 00:20:38,104
The distant shooting star we saw.

286
00:20:38,104 --> 00:20:41,894
haato no puromisu

287
00:20:38,104 --> 00:20:41,894
Believe in our promise. As much as you'd call it true love.

288
00:20:41,894 --> 00:20:51,694
ai to ieru hodo shinjite

289
00:20:41,894 --> 00:20:51,694
You stop, as if you'd do that...

290
00:20:50,444 --> 00:20:55,704
Don't be shy, we've got lots of sake and food, so please speak up if you want more!

291
00:20:56,704 --> 00:20:58,074
Sorry to bother you.

292
00:20:58,074 --> 00:21:00,794
A bunch of guys who can drink to their heart's content here.

293
00:21:00,794 --> 00:21:02,664
What are you saying?

294
00:21:01,704 --> 00:21:04,874
kaze ni yureru kami osaeru you ni

295
00:21:01,704 --> 00:21:04,874
...to keep your hair from fluttering in the wind.

296
00:21:02,664 --> 00:21:08,504
Letting me serve you sake to fill you up on the day of the festival is my pleasure.

297
00:21:04,874 --> 00:21:06,924
kimi wa tomadoi

298
00:21:04,874 --> 00:21:06,924
I painted my cheeks red...

299
00:21:07,174 --> 00:21:12,264
koi no hajimari to kidukanai de hoo wo akakushita

300
00:21:07,174 --> 00:21:12,264
...so I wouldn't notice that I had fallen in love.

301
00:21:08,504 --> 00:21:09,674
But!

302
00:21:09,674 --> 00:21:13,304
I won't forgive you if you drink too much and ruin the place.

303
00:21:12,594 --> 00:21:15,724
ikusen no hikari ryoute de hora

304
00:21:12,594 --> 00:21:15,724
You have myriads of light rays in your hand.

305
00:21:15,724 --> 00:21:17,804
hoshi wo sukutte

306
00:21:15,724 --> 00:21:17,804
Come on and save that star.

307
00:21:18,014 --> 00:21:21,354
hitori no yoru demo waraeru you ni

308
00:21:18,014 --> 00:21:21,354
So you can smile even on a night when you're alone.

309
00:21:21,354 --> 00:21:26,644
omoi de wo hanabi ni shite

310
00:21:21,354 --> 00:21:26,644
Turn them into fireworks of your memories.

311
00:21:21,434 --> 00:21:26,644
But, to think we would see another confession during the calling-out ceremony...

312
00:21:26,854 --> 00:21:31,524
kimi to boku no uta ni nare

313
00:21:26,854 --> 00:21:31,524
And let them become a song for us.

314
00:21:27,404 --> 00:21:30,944
It reminds me of what you did back then.

315
00:21:31,734 --> 00:21:34,654
saa ten made todoke kono kimochi

316
00:21:31,734 --> 00:21:34,654
Let the heavens know...

317
00:21:32,614 --> 00:21:35,784
Sadly, you were rejected, right?

318
00:21:35,074 --> 00:21:37,244
kokoro wo gyutto tsunagou

319
00:21:35,074 --> 00:21:37,244
...about our love that connects us firmly.

320
00:21:35,784 --> 00:21:39,244
Gen-san, that's a personal matter.

321
00:21:37,244 --> 00:21:40,374
yowakutatte iin da boku no te de

322
00:21:37,244 --> 00:21:40,374
It's okay if you're weak.

323
00:21:40,584 --> 00:21:43,294
sono yume wo hippatte iku

324
00:21:40,584 --> 00:21:43,294
I'll grab your hand and realise your dream.

325
00:21:42,834 --> 00:21:43,704
Another glass!

326
00:21:43,294 --> 00:21:45,874
kakehashi ni na itai yo

327
00:21:43,294 --> 00:21:45,874
I want to become your only bridge.

328
00:21:44,164 --> 00:21:48,924
Erm, dear Mother, it seems like you've had quite a bit to drink. Any more would be...

329
00:21:45,874 --> 00:21:53,514
kimi hitori no kirari niji ni naru deshou

330
00:21:45,874 --> 00:21:53,514
I'm sure we will be shining forever...

331
00:21:49,584 --> 00:21:50,714
Huh?!

332
00:21:52,384 --> 00:21:55,174
You got something to say to your mother?!

333
00:21:53,764 --> 00:22:00,094
boku ni kimi wo eien ni

334
00:21:53,764 --> 00:22:00,094
...brightly like a rainbow.

335
00:21:55,174 --> 00:22:01,104
I only drink so much in the first place
because you cause me so much trouble!

336
00:22:01,104 --> 00:22:02,604
Do you get it?

337
00:22:03,314 --> 00:22:05,144
Understood!

338
00:22:04,724 --> 00:22:06,314
Most probably both of us...

339
00:22:04,724 --> 00:22:06,314
tabun bokutachi wa

340
00:22:06,314 --> 00:22:10,234
...are searching for a better tomorrow with our bare hands.

341
00:22:06,314 --> 00:22:10,234
tesaguri shite ashita wo motome

342
00:22:06,314 --> 00:22:08,444
Well then, fill 'er up!

343
00:22:08,444 --> 00:22:09,904
Yes!

344
00:22:10,234 --> 00:22:13,484
The times we get angry and the times we feel sad,

345
00:22:10,234 --> 00:22:13,484
toki ni okottari naitari shite

346
00:22:10,484 --> 00:22:11,824
Eh?

347
00:22:11,824 --> 00:22:13,964
Ayumu, you're an artist!

348
00:22:13,484 --> 00:22:15,614
become the scars in our heart.

349
00:22:13,484 --> 00:22:15,614
kizuna ni kaeru yo

350
00:22:13,964 --> 00:22:16,864
Could I have you draw one of me next time?

351
00:22:15,614 --> 00:22:21,164
Although our future isn't written in the horoscopes.

352
00:22:15,614 --> 00:22:21,164
Horoscope ni wa mirai chizu wa kaitenai kedo

353
00:22:17,284 --> 00:22:21,704
Even though I look like this, when I'm nude, I'm actually pretty great.

354
00:22:21,164 --> 00:22:24,374
We both pointed at the vast sky.

355
00:22:21,164 --> 00:22:24,374
futari yubisashita oozora ni wa

356
00:22:21,704 --> 00:22:22,954
Eh?

357
00:22:24,374 --> 00:22:29,964
It's the start of a story.

358
00:22:24,374 --> 00:22:29,964
monogatari no hajimari ga

359
00:22:29,964 --> 00:22:34,884
The birth of it can be heard already.

360
00:22:29,964 --> 00:22:34,884
ubugoe wo ageru deshou

361
00:22:34,674 --> 00:22:37,304
What's up with that thing, Koyo-nee?

362
00:22:34,884 --> 00:22:37,974
Come on, let's fly up the shining hill.

363
00:22:34,884 --> 00:22:37,974
saa kagayaku oka de tobitatou

364
00:22:37,674 --> 00:22:38,844
It's nice, isn't it?

365
00:22:37,974 --> 00:22:40,394
Come along with me.

366
00:22:37,974 --> 00:22:40,394
boku ni tsuiteoide

367
00:22:38,844 --> 00:22:40,644
I got it while playing ring toss at the festival!

368
00:22:40,394 --> 00:22:46,354
Even if you cry, I will protect you with these wings of mine.

369
00:22:40,394 --> 00:22:46,354
tatoe namida shite mo kono tsubasa nurasanu you ni tsutsumu kara

370
00:22:41,594 --> 00:22:43,264
That's quite cute-

371
00:22:43,264 --> 00:22:43,854
Ah!

372
00:22:46,354 --> 00:22:51,314
"I will always walk the same path as you."

373
00:22:46,354 --> 00:22:51,314
ãonnaji michi wo zutto aruite yukouã

374
00:22:49,394 --> 00:22:51,444
Don't touch that part!

375
00:22:51,314 --> 00:22:56,824
I'm sorry, but I don't want you to find me.

376
00:22:51,314 --> 00:22:56,824
gomen mitsukaranain da

377
00:22:55,944 --> 00:22:57,364
This is very delicious!

378
00:22:56,824 --> 00:23:03,374
To say anything beyond this...

379
00:22:56,824 --> 00:23:03,374
kore ijou no kotoba nante...

380
00:22:57,944 --> 00:23:00,154
Mugi-nee, didn't you have a stomach ache?

381
00:23:00,704 --> 00:23:02,624
My, did I?

382
00:23:11,294 --> 00:23:14,174
We were rejected.

383
00:23:14,174 --> 00:23:15,594
That's right.

384
00:23:16,634 --> 00:23:22,734
I wasn't really rejected or anything.

385
00:23:22,734 --> 00:23:23,264
Hmm?

386
00:23:29,104 --> 00:23:30,894
Well, whatever.

387
00:23:45,204 --> 00:23:46,534
Wow!

388
00:23:47,084 --> 00:23:48,414
We saw it, huh?

389
00:23:48,414 --> 00:23:50,294
The bridge that leads to the starry sky.

390
00:23:53,374 --> 00:23:55,794
It's beautiful.

391
00:23:56,884 --> 00:23:58,054
That's right.

392
00:23:58,514 --> 00:23:59,964
You <i>are</i> very beautiful.

